   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "FINAL_V2 / 1b - ADD A CAMERA PATH TO AN EXISTING DATASET (incremental SfM)\n\nCompanion to 1_camera_plot_flythrough. Use this AFTER you already built a SphereSfM dataset (with workflow 1) and want to ADD more coverage without redoing everything.\n\nONE 'Camera Plot Fly-Through + Geometry Overlay' node plots a new path, renders its equirect control video and drives ONE WAN branch. The decoded WAN frames feed the 'SphereSfM Add Camera Path to Dataset' node, which REGISTERS them into the existing reconstruction (colmap_sphere image_registrator -> point_triangulator -> cube reprojection) and grows images/ + sparse/0 in place.\n\nPOINT IT AT THE DATASET: set the Dataset Project node's name to the SAME dataset you built with workflow 1 (its dataset_dir feeds the add node). That dataset must still have its _spheresfm_work/ folder (it does if workflow 1 ran with mode=colmap_now).\n\nMAKE IT LINK UP: start the new path NEAR where the earlier paths looked so SfM can match features across them, and keep real camera MOVEMENT/parallax. If none of the new frames register, move the start closer to the existing views or raise max_num_features.\n\nBy default existing cameras stay FIXED (purely additive). Flip adjust_existing_cameras on only if you want the new data to also refine the original poses (re-renders all faces). Run this BEFORE upscaling. Chainable: run again to add a 3rd, 4th, ... path.\n\nTRAIN (pinhole COLMAP, NO --gut):\n  LichtFeld-Studio.exe -d <model_dir> -o <out> --headless --train --strategy mcmc --max-cap 2000000 --sh-degree 2"
   ],
   "color": "#234",
   "bgcolor": "#355"
  },
